.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt EGGHEAD-INIT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm egghead-init
.Nd first-run setup wizard
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm egghead init
.Op Fl -dry-run
.Op Fl -config Ar path
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Cm init
wizard walks through the three things every new install needs:
the records directory, at least one LLM provider, and a default
model. It writes the result to
.Pa ~/.config/egghead/config.yml
(respecting
.Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
and
.Ev EGGHEAD_CONFIG ) ,
creating the records directory if it does not exist.
.Pp
.Cm init
is safe to re-run. When a configuration file already exists, the
wizard prompts before overwriting and shows existing values as
defaults.
.Pp
On hosts that support a user-scope service supervisor, the wizard
offers to install one at the end so
.Cm egghead serve
survives logout and restarts on failure. See
.Xr egghead-service 1 .
.Pp
The wizard knows about Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, xAI, Groq, DeepSeek,
Mistral, OpenRouter, Ollama, LM Studio, and any custom OpenAI-compatible
endpoint. API keys can be entered directly or referenced from the
environment via the
.Sy {env:VAR}
substitution syntax described in
.Xr egghead 5 .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--config path"
.It Fl -dry-run
Print the configuration that would be written without saving it.
The records directory is also not created.
.It Fl -config Ar path
Save the configuration to a custom path instead of the XDG default.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Show help.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Default setup:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
egghead init
.Ed
.Pp
Save to a project-scoped configuration:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
egghead init --config ~/projects/my-kb/egghead.yml
.Ed
.Pp
Preview without writing:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
egghead init --dry-run
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr egghead-config 1 ,
.Xr egghead-llm 1 ,
.Xr egghead-doctor 1 ,
.Xr egghead-service 1 ,
.Xr egghead 1 ,
.Xr egghead 5
